---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-phone-field</code> takes a phone number. The country selector at its start shows the flag
  and calling code; the field takes the national number. <code>value</code> is the whole number in
  E.164 form, such as <code>+442079460958</code>, or empty while the field holds no valid number.
  Paste or type a full international number (<code>+44 20 7946 0958</code>) and the field selects
  its country.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 360px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-phone-field id='phone-field-demo' label='Phone' name='phone' required></wc-phone-field>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#phone-field-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change :: ' + event.detail.value + ' (' + event.detail.country + ')');
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Countries</h3>
<p>
  <code>country</code> (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2) starts as the region of the page's locale, else
  <code>US</code>. <code>countries</code> limits and orders the list; <code>preferred-countries</code>
  pins the likely ones above the rest. Countries that share a calling code, such as the +1 countries,
  keep the one the person selected.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 360px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-phone-field
      label='Mobile'
      country='GB'
      preferred-countries='["GB", "IE", "FR"]'
      value='+447700900123'
    ></wc-phone-field>
    <wc-phone-field label='Office (Nordics)' countries='["SE", "NO", "DK", "FI", "IS"]'></wc-phone-field>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Validation</h3>
<p>
  The field checks the shape of the number, not whether it exists: digits, with spaces, dashes and
  brackets allowed between them, and 4 to 15 digits with the calling code. Anything else shows
  "Enter a valid phone number" once the value is committed, and blocks form submission.
</p>
